<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 7 April, from 529 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">529</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian promulgates the first Code of Roman law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Justinian issued the Codex Justinianus, gathering imperial constitutions into a single authoritative collection. Revised in 534, it became the core of the Corpus Juris Civilis that shaped European law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1348</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles IV founds the university in Prague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles IV, King of Bohemia, issued the charter founding a university in Prague, the first in Central Europe. Now Charles University, it later became a centre of the Hussite reform movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1739</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Highwayman Dick Turpin is hanged at York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dick Turpin, convicted of horse theft, was hanged on the Knavesmire at York. The violent robber was later romanticised in fiction as a dashing gentleman of the road.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1798</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates the Mississippi Territory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Congress organised the Mississippi Territory on land ceded by Spain in 1795. It was later enlarged and divided into the states of Mississippi and Alabama.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1827</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Walker records the first sale of friction matches</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stockton-on-Tees chemist John Walker sold his newly invented 'friction lights', matches struck against sandpaper. He never patented them, and others soon copied the idea.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1939</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy invades Albania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mussolini's forces landed at Durrës and other ports, and within days King Zog had fled. Albania was joined to the Italian crown, and the invasion later served as a base for Italy's attack on Greece.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1994</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genocide against the Tutsi begins in Rwanda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hours after President Habyarimana's aircraft was shot down, extremists began killing Tutsi and moderate Hutu. In about 100 days an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 people were murdered.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">Genocide</a></div></li></ol>
